# Aggregating reads of a duplicate-bearing lake table that are exempt
# from scripts/ci/lint-lake-dedup.sh.
#
# Format: `<file>:<stellar.table>  <reason>`, one per line. The key is
# printed by the gate on failure, so an entry is copied rather than
# hand-derived. The reason field is REQUIRED.
#
# SHRINK-ONLY. Adding a line needs a `Baseline-Growth:` commit trailer
# naming this file (scripts/ci/lint-baseline-growth.sh), and a line
# whose site no longer violates is STALE and fails the gate until it is
# deleted.
#
# Every entry below counts physical rows on purpose, tests only for
# emptiness, or reads a table that is not a ReplacingMergeTree; the
# reason says which.
test/integration/clickhouse_accounts_test.go:stellar.transactions  counts the physical versions of each key: the precondition that both versions exist before FINAL is tested
test/integration/clickhouse_accounts_test.go:stellar.operations  counts the physical versions of each key: the precondition that both versions exist before FINAL is tested
test/integration/clickhouse_lake_test.go:stellar.account_movements  asserts the physical rows one fixture insert wrote; FINAL would hide a writer that emits a row twice
test/integration/clickhouse_rollups_test.go:stellar.movements_by_asset  asserts the catch-up wrote no physical row for a stale key
deploy/clickhouse/contract_event_shapes.sql:stellar.contract_events  the shape table's cnt is a discovery weight, stated in the file as only ever raised by overlap; a materialized view cannot read FINAL
deploy/clickhouse/tier1_schema.sql:stellar.contract_events  the same contract_event_shapes view as contract_event_shapes.sql
internal/storage/clickhouse/recognition.go:stellar.contract_events  cnt only orders shapes for recognition and is never served as a count; FINAL over the whole window would more than double a bounded discovery scan
test/integration/clickhouse_reads_test.go:stellar.contract_events  an EXPLAIN of the planner's granule pruning, not a count that is read
internal/storage/clickhouse/contiguity_reader.go:stellar.ledgers  count() is the physical row total on purpose: DuplicateRows() = count() - uniqExact(ledger_seq) is the duplicate surplus the contiguity check reports
internal/storage/clickhouse/contracts_census.go:stellar.%s  the %s is the census's private staging copy of stellar.contracts_census_daily, a plain MergeTree filled by one INSERT
internal/storage/clickhouse/participant_backfill.go:stellar.operation_participants  count() only tests emptiness (cnt == 0), which a duplicate cannot change; an unfiltered count() is answered from part metadata, FINAL would merge the table
internal/storage/clickhouse/sponsorship_totals.go:stellar.sponsorship_events  count() only tests emptiness (n > 0), which a duplicate cannot change; an unfiltered count() is answered from part metadata
test/integration/clickhouse_accounts_test.go:stellar.ledger_entry_changes  the fixture purge counts physical rows before and after DELETE; FINAL would hide a surviving version
test/integration/clickhouse_entries_test.go:stellar.ledger_entry_changes  count() only tests whether the lake is empty, which a duplicate cannot change
test/integration/clickhouse_reads_test.go:stellar.ledger_entry_changes  counts the physical versions of one key: the precondition that the stale twin exists unmerged
test/integration/clickhouse_reads_test.go:stellar.entry_history_watermark  asserts a lower mark wrote no physical row; FINAL would hide the extra version under test
